# Inter-segment firewall allow-list for the range router (VMID 9200).
#
# Default policy between segments is DENY. Every line here opens one hole in the
# router's forward chain. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# Format (whitespace-separated):
#     <src_segment>  <dst_segment>  <proto>  <dport>
#
#   src_segment / dst_segment : a "name" from segments.json, or "any"
#   proto                     : tcp | udp | icmp | any
#   dport                     : destination port, a range a-b, or "any"
#                               (ignored for proto icmp/any)
#
# Stateful: the reply direction is allowed automatically (ct established,related).
# Only the initiating direction needs a rule.
#
# After editing, re-apply with:   ./configure_router.py segments.json
#
# Examples (uncomment to use):
# user    server  tcp  443      # user segment may reach https on servers
# user    server  icmp any      # user segment may ping servers
# any     server  tcp  53       # anyone may reach DNS on a server box
